# Client API handoff rules

When editing `app/**/handoff/*.md` or `app/base/handoff/*.md`:

- Write for frontend/mobile developers, not backend maintainers.
- Include method, path, auth requirement, params, request JSON, response JSON fields, status codes, and error shapes.
- Document the standard response envelope, pagination shape, and rate-limit headers/429 response where relevant.
- Never include migrations, SQL, Tortoise internals, internal file paths, or deployment-only implementation details.
- Verify endpoint paths and auth/role markers against live route registration before marking a flow complete.
